<title>GERMANY: TABLE-Dresdner details H1 results.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Dresdner details H1 results.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group oper profit after risk provs    1,743  vs 1,417</p>
<p>Group net income from financial</p>
<p>    transactions				  572.9  vs 382.2</p>
<p>Group risk provisions in lending</p>
<p>    business					610.7  vs 508.8</p>
<p>    Group net interest income		 3,693  vs 3,365</p>
<p>    Group net commission income	     2,553  vs 1,905</p>
<p>Group net income from securities held</p>
<p>    in liquidity portfolio		    270.7  vs 366.4</p>
<p>    Group balance sheet total		 645,530 vs 561,163</p>
<p>    Group lending volume			342,669 vs 322,791</p>
<p>    BIS equity capital ratio		  9.6 pct vs 9.4 pct</p>
<p>    Group staff (headcount)		   45,396  vs 45,816</p>
<p>    Branches					1,583   vs 1,576</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German bank is Dresdner Bank AG.</p>
<p>The bank earlier released a rounded figure for its group operating profit after risk provisions of &quot;over 1.7 billion marks.&quot;</p>
<p>Earnings compare with first half of 1996. Balance sheet total, lending volume and capital ratio compare June 30, 1997 with December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>Dresdner said its net income from financial transactions in the first half of 1997 amounted to almost 90 percent of the entire full-year income in that segment.</p>
<p>Securities trade contributed 145.4 million marks, income from currency and precious metals trading contributed 163.2 million marks and trade in other financial instruments contributed 264.3 million marks, Dresdner said.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
